## Generic Axis Lengths

Slices are used to define generic functions that manipulate arrays with any number of axes of any lengths.

For example: 
```
func add[Shape []int](float32, [Shape...]float32) [Shape...]float32
```
defines an `add` function with one generic argument, `Shape` of type `[]int`, and which takes two non-generic (runtime) arguments: a `float32` scalar, and an array of `float32` with any number of axes. `add` returns an array with the same shape. We use `Shape...` to expand the slice `Shape` to multiple axis lengths.

The `add` function can then be called with different array shapes as in the example.
